Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10. Next rigorous extension for OPF specifically", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5ec5fe12-9a23-294f-ae7a-5b0e15c5fe9a"],

Cell["\<\
To connect this notebook back to the OPF derivation, the next mathematically \
meaningful steps are:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"55efeb23-55d2-ac4e-8b64-cea16b25c41f"],

Cell["\<\
1. add a true time-dependent kinetic structure to the OPF action\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f5da6c28-4698-8d4c-8db2-464a403f92d6"],

Cell["\<\
2. derive the linearized field operator around a nontrivial equilibrium\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11353136-d99d-804d-9c62-09fd09fb3274"],

Cell["3. compute its modal spectrum", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12d34c98-f6fa-d247-b99b-1d7f4c870657"],

Cell["\<\
4. define an explicit coarse-graining transform on the field variables or \
couplings\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"403bbfc5-d80c-7e41-9501-03ec7fe08418"],

Cell["\<\
5. define a measurement/decoherence channel on the mode amplitudes\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30e5f87d-2c8b-3a47-b60b-3afd6efc7ae5"],

Cell["6. test whether the same modes are: ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d706f13-beff-aa4b-95b4-b0550654ff69"],

Cell["spectrally stable,", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"7bc88a9c-7e45-b444-b864-04951af0ba90"],

Cell["RG-persistent,", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"b20b25cb-1f61-4248-aa1d-35f6db86ac50"],

Cell["pointer-selected", "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"510926b7-28ab-0045-8036-56b6d5e582f8"],

Cell["\<\
Only then can the proposed synthesis be evaluated as more than an analogy. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d983ffd-9701-c04d-80d7-a8dba28eeee9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
